# Reference observations for run_validation.py --compare. Copy to
# data/reference_observations.csv (gitignored) and fill with real data.
#
# location: Must match a location name in validation/config.py exactly
#           (quote it, since names contain a comma: "Berlin, Germany")
# year:     Observation year
# event:    "leaf" (compared with the SI-x leaf index) or "bloom" (SI-x bloom index)
# species:  Latin name of the observed species. SI-x models lilac
#           (Syringa vulgaris); other species are compared but not equivalent.
# doy:      Day of year (1-366), usually the median over nearby stations
# n_obs:    Number of station observations behind the median
# source:   Data network (e.g. DWD, SLU)
# notes:    Phase code / BBCH stage, search radius, range, license
#
# Use only openly licensed sources (DWD: CC BY 4.0, SLU Naturens Kalender: CC0).
# PEP725 and ECA&D are non-commercial only; don't mix them in here.
#
# EXAMPLE ROWS (real 2020 values; replace with your own)
"Berlin, Germany",2020,bloom,Syringa vulgaris,116,14,DWD,"Median of annual-reporter stations within 0.5 deg, phase 5 (beginning of flowering). CC BY 4.0."
"Stockholm, Sweden",2020,bloom,Syringa vulgaris,148,3,SLU,"Median of observations within 1 deg, phase 53 (start of flowering, BBCH 61). CC0."
"Stockholm, Sweden",2020,leaf,Syringa vulgaris,111.5,2,SLU,"Lilac first leaf, phase 33 (BBCH 11). CC0."
"Stockholm, Sweden",2020,leaf,Betula pendula,121,12,SLU,"Median within 1 deg, phase 33 (BBCH 11), quality-0 rows excluded. CC0."
